1. An analysis method for a magnetic field of a coaxial solenoid cylinder generating a uniform magnetic field, characterized by comprising the following steps:
S1: deriving, based on the fundamental Maxwell theory, mathematical models of magnetic field distributions within a barrel bore of a coaxial solenoid under different excitation types;
S2: establishing, by using Ansoft Maxwell, a numerical electromagnetic field simulation model of a closely wound solenoid cylinder;
S3: performing simulation analysis on induced magnetic fields within the barrel at different external excitation frequencies; and
S4: with excitation conditions kept unchanged, increasing magnetic flux density inside the cylinder by optimizing coil parameters;
wherein, in S2, for an alternating magnetic field, when a metal component having relatively high magnetic permeability is present in the magnetic field, an eddy-current solver of a magnetic field module is adopted in Maxwell software, Eddy-current under Magnetic is selected, a Cartesian coordinate system is adopted, and a length unit is mm; in consideration of continuity of a tangential component of magnetic field intensity H and a normal component of magnetic flux density B between contact surfaces of different objects under natural boundary conditions, the contact surfaces between the objects are set as natural boundary conditions; according to characteristics of Neumann boundary conditions, the magnetic field intensity H is tangent to a boundary surface, and a normal component of the magnetic field intensity is 0; a solution region is set as air; a cross section is defined at any portion of the solenoid model, current excitation is applied, and a solution setting is added; and the coil model is meshed, wherein a maximum edge length of a cylinder mesh is defined as 3.5 mm, and a maximum edge length of a coil mesh is 0.2 mm.

